1133	//  THIN ORIENTATION WRAPPERS over tc_gemm_block_unpipelined. These reproduce
1134	//  the THREE accessor patterns the engine is silicon-validated on
1135	//  (decoder_tc_selftest.cu / test_decoder_tc.py 13/13): fwd (Y=X·Wᵀ, no
1136	//  transpose), dX (dX=dY·W, W transposed-staged), dW (dW=dYᵀ·X, BOTH
1137	//  transposed-staged, K=T). The driver calls THESE — it never re-derives the
1138	//  staging (the no-suppression / reuse-the-validated-unit discipline).
1139	//
1140	//  All operands are HBM bf16 row-major. The caller passes one A(64×16) + one
1141	//  B(Nmax×16) smem staging pair (the engine reuses them across k-steps). N is
1142	//  the compile-time wgmma atom width (128 for in/out/ff dX-N=d; the fwd loops
1143	//  N-tiles internally). Accumulation is fp32; output written via the accessor.
